WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.382
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 5: Tell Me How.

2
00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:06.772
Unit 5 turns you into a writer of instructions.

3
00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:12.830
You will take apart a Somali recipe for
bariis to see how a title, a materials list,

4
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.528
numbered steps and tips work together,
and you will learn the zero conditional,

5
00:00:18.608 --> 00:00:22.639
the pattern that explains what happens every single time.

6
00:00:22.719 --> 00:00:26.462
Alongside the recipe you will read “The Memory Wall”,

7
00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:31.367
a story about a class who learn to
communicate what matters to them.

8
00:00:31.447 --> 00:00:34.396
By the end you will have planned, drafted,

9
00:00:34.476 --> 00:00:40.743
tested and revised your own set of instructions
that somebody else can genuinely follow.

10
00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:46.801
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:46.881 --> 00:00:53.385
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
read procedural and instructional texts closely,

12
00:00:53.465 --> 00:00:58.765
naming their key features and explaining
how the structure helps the reader.

13
00:00:58.845 --> 00:01:04.429
You will also recognise imperative verbs
such as rinse, stir, place and measure,

14
00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:07.402
and open your own written steps with them.

15
00:01:07.482 --> 00:01:12.641
You will also identify and use time
connectives such as first, next, then,

16
00:01:12.721 --> 00:01:16.110
after that and finally to sequence steps clearly.

17
00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.729
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

18
00:01:18.809 --> 00:01:25.104
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: communicate,
quote, emphasise, persuade, convince, encourage.

19
00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:29.929
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

20
00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:33.683
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

21
00:01:33.763 --> 00:01:39.371
The reading sequence includes What Makes
Instructions Work and How to Make Bariis: Spiced Rice.

22
00:01:39.451 --> 00:01:40.209
Read actively.

23
00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:44.340
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:48.232
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:01:48.312 --> 00:01:52.265
The first language focus is What the Zero Conditional Is For.

26
00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:56.827
The zero conditional describes
results that follow every single time.

27
00:01:56.907 --> 00:01:59.405
Scientists reach for it to state facts,

28
00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:06.083
and instruction writers reach for it to explain
what happens when a step is done properly or skipped.

29
00:02:06.163 --> 00:02:13.289
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

30
00:02:13.369 --> 00:02:17.840
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: The Instruction Game (Pairs).

31
00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.074
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

32
00:02:22.154 --> 00:02:25.297
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

33
00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:28.647
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

34
00:02:28.727 --> 00:02:30.257
You are ready to begin.

35
00:02:30.337 --> 00:02:37.184
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

36
00:02:37.264 --> 00:02:40.543
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

37
00:02:40.623 --> 00:02:48.450
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
